    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Marc Britten",
        "email": "11667518+marcbritten@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-22T16:30:46Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Marc Britten",
        "email": "11667518+marcbritten@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-22T16:33:35Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(project): save a project through a temp file and a rename\n\nproject::save wrote the project with std::fs::write. That call truncates\nthe old file first. A write that stopped (a full disk, a lost network\nshare, a stopped app) left a damaged project and no old copy.\n\nproject::save now writes through machine::store::write_atomic: a temp\nfile in the same folder, flushed, then renamed over the target. Machine\nfiles, preferences, recent files and view settings already use it. The\nwindow, the MCP tool save_project and the script call cam.save all go\nthrough project::save.\n\nTwo refusals of the plain write stay. A folder that does not exist is\nrefused by name, because write_atomic creates missing folders. A\nread-only project file is refused by name, because on Linux and macOS a\nrename replaces a read-only file.\n\nmachine::store::temp_path_for gives the temp path. write_atomic uses it,\nand the tests use it to make a save fail. A path that names no file is\nnow refused by name before a folder is made.\n\nFixes #3509\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
