      "committer": {
        "name": "Marc Britten",
        "email": "11667518+marcbritten@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-22T17:08:34Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(machine): give each thread its own temp file name\n\nThe temp file of write_atomic had only the process ID in its name. Two\nsaves of one file at the same moment (an autosave and a save by the\nuser) thus wrote the same temp file.\n\nThe name now also has a number for the calling thread. Each thread\ntakes its number one time, from one counter. Two saves at the same\nmoment run on two threads, so they write two temp files. The saves of\none thread run one after another, so its name can repeat, and a test\ncan still put a folder in the place of the temp file.\n\nThe new test two_threads_never_share_a_temp_file pins the names.\n\nRefs #3509\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
