      "message": "fix(project): probe write access before the atomic save\n\n`project::save` now opens an existing project file for writing, with no\ntruncate and no create, before it writes the temp file. A file that this\nprocess cannot write is refused as read-only, so the rename never replaces\nit. This pins the shared-folder case: alice owns `/shared/job.camproj`\nwith mode 0644, bob saves from CamCraft, and alice's project stays.\n`Permissions::readonly()` alone misses that file on Unix, because its mode\nhas a write bit and the rename needs write permission on the folder only.\n\nThe missing-folder refusal and the temp-file and rename stay unchanged.\n\nTests: `a_project_save_over_a_unix_socket_is_refused_and_kept` (red\nbefore the probe: the rename replaced the socket) and\n`a_project_save_into_a_folder_without_write_access_is_refused_and_kept`.\nThe cross-user case needs another uid and is not pinned.\n\nRefs #3509\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
